{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I have also heard, etc.</b> Its saying <b>also</b> means: besides that they prayed to the attribute of mercy, and besides the love of the fathers and their covenant, there is a third aspect — namely, their outcry alone, apart from the bondage, HaShem heard the sound of their outcry of heart-pain. And this is what it says <b>and also I</b>; and the meaning of ״I״ is the name of mercy, as He said at the outset: ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו אֲנִי ה׳״ (Exodus 6:2) — from the side of My mercy alone I have heard their groaning, meaning, an outcry of heart-pain like a wounded person who groans without need of their prayer. And this is what He was precise in saying <b>that the Egyptians are enslaving them</b> — meaning, the aspect of the pain of the bondage that the Egyptians are inflicting upon them is what I have heard. And see what I explained on the verse (Exodus 2:23): ״וַתַּעַל שַׁוְעָתָם אֶל הָאֱלֹהִים מִן הָעֲבוֹדָה״. It also fits according to the other approaches that we have written, and the discerning one will understand." "<b>And I have remembered My covenant.</b> This also means to redeem them, to give them the land, and it is the covenant recorded in the immediate context. And I am advancing it at this time to the side of mercy, as we wrote above. And if one says that the covenant is to exact punishment from the offending nation — this covenant was not mentioned in the immediate context, and it is far-fetched to push the matter so far."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:06.163084997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}